The design rests on a live-JVM oracle IN THE TREE: conformance/ws_j_index_fidelity_conformance_test.go (two Describes, "WS-J index-definition fidelity oracle" and "WS-J literal-width query oracle", in target //conformance:rfc257_oracle_test, hand-maintained in conformance/BUILD.bazel), its harvested corpus conformance/testdata/rfc257/java_index_templates.json and harvester rfcs/257-java-upgrade-audit/ws-j-oracle/harvest.py, shared helpers conformance/index_shape_helpers_test.go (moved verbatim out of index_ddl_metadata_conformance_test.go and metadata_proto_conformance_test.go; both targets compile it). Evidence: rfcs/257-java-upgrade-audit/ws-j-oracle/ (README, evidence-run.txt = full-target run, evidence-mutations.txt). 118 runs, every Java outcome pinned; Go recorded.
One production change is ALREADY in the tree and is part of this review: the field-path trie fix in pkg/relational/core/query/ddl/generator.go computeTrieAtDepth (prefix check before length check), pinned by pkg/relational/core/embedded/index_ddl_field_trie_test.go. Everything else in the design is not implemented yet.
Tree objects: run `git show TREE:path` from the repo root (the read-only policy admits commands that START with the git subcommand, or `git -C /home/birdy/projects/fdb-go ...`; avoid shell variables and `cd ... &&` chains). Java tag 4.14.2.0 at fdacd162a9c8acfadc49082b89185c823ab8ae4a in fdb-record-layer/ (read fdb-record-layer/.git/HEAD if rev-parse is denied).
Read the FULL design, the oracle spec, harvester, evidence and the trie fix, and check every claim against actual Java (DdlVisitor.visitCreateSchemaTemplateStatement/visitEnumDefinition, RecordLayerSchemaTemplate(.Builder/.accept), RecordLayerTable.accept, FileDescriptorSerializer, RecordMetadataSerializer, RecordMetaData.toProto, RecordMetaDataBuilder.build, the query/ddl package: MaterializedViewIndexGenerator, IndexSpec, QuantifierValues, ValueToKeyExpressionVisitor, OnSourceIndexGenerator, FieldValueTrieNode, FieldValue.ResolvedAccessor, ArithmeticValue, SemanticAnalyzer bitmap arity, SchemaExistsBehavior, RecordLayerStoreCatalog saveSchema/repairSchema/initialize, RecordLayerCreateSchemaConstantAction, CopyPlan) and current Go (pkg/relational/core/query/ddl, core/metadata/builder.go, embedded/ddl.go and cascades_generator.go buildSchemaTemplateFromDDL, core/catalog fdb_store_catalog.go and store_catalog.go, core/ddl/create_schema.go, api/catalog.go, expr/expr.go ResolveConstant and walk.go bitmap injection, values scalar_function_catalog.go and ArithmeticValue lanes). Challenge: completeness against the umbrella and audit; whether each finding is real and each fix is the Java-aligned one; the wire claims (record-type keys, union field numbers, index versions, literal carriers) and their consequences; the declared non-ports (record_types order, anonymous names) and the canonicalization that backs them; the oracle's integrity (harvest completeness, derived-body cut, pin/set guards, what it cannot see); the existence-policy concurrency claim; test sufficiency (mutation-checkable, FDB-backed). Distinguish measured target facts from source hypotheses.
Preserved boundaries: approved Go read/raw nullable-array, scalar and sorting extensions; RFC-209 group-existence companions; the rebind validator; one Cascades pipeline; C++ 7.3.77; format max 15 / default 14.
Actual reviewer gate run via `claude -p` (model opus, effort xhigh) under a read-only tool policy (Read/Grep/Glob plus read-only git/grep/sed Bash; no Edit/Write). The owner authorized this substitution for the exhausted Codex account. No tests/probes/mutations/edits/staging/commits/push/CI/PR/publication/operational changes. Return ACK or NAK, the exact tree and design hash, and actionable findings with source line references ordered by severity. Incomplete review is not ACK. Under 900 words unless needed.

